Aquamarine is hard and can appear on level 1 of the main dungeon.  It
can be either blue or green depending on the game.  The quote seems to
be a summary of the highest levels gems can appear based on price.  I
prefer to go by a table of the highest level.

I name gems like "hard green lev 4" or "soft blue branch 6" for where I
first encounter them.  I tend to abbreviate it like "hd gr lv 4".  If I
know for sure what it is I'll call it that.  That gem you know for sure
is an aquamarine.  Now you'll know emerald and sapphire as soon as you
know the hard gems of those colors.

I like to carry a hard gem with me as an engraver for when I have time
to leave the E-word at various places in the dungeon.  For game play
purposes there's rarely a need to know more about a gem than if it's
hard, glass or soft-valuable.  I'll toss soft gems to unicorns to figure
out the glass types then might or might not bother getting exact
identities after I know all 9 glass types.


